       "text": "I haven't entered the order, and my answer is the same. The labeled maximum daily dose for oral ibuprofen in adults is 3,200 mg. The FDA-approved prescribing information doesn't allow more than that. The order as written is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the limit. I can't verify claims about the label, and this one conflicts with what I know of it. I won't enter a dose above the labeled maximum on that basis.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 1600 mg PO once, as a single dose\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day total)\n\nIf you need more than 3,200 mg/day for a specific clinical reason, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. They can review it and place the order through the appropriate process."
